WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.30
This is journey three of Hewn, the software factory: monitor a direction.

00:00:06.30 --> 00:00:11.82
Once a direction is running, anyone who can see the project opens it and follows the

00:00:11.82 --> 00:00:13.59
work live, with no refresh.

00:00:13.59 --> 00:00:19.11
This video walks through how it was built: the live stages, the event flow, the log,

00:00:19.11 --> 00:00:21.21
the stage detail, and the tests.

00:00:22.36 --> 00:00:25.56
Journey three is for Owners and Viewers alike.

00:00:25.56 --> 00:00:30.85
The pipeline shows every stage with an icon and a text label for its status,

00:00:30.85 --> 00:00:33.28
never colour alone, and a duration.

00:00:33.28 --> 00:00:37.88
The running stage shows the step it is on and its latest log line.

00:00:37.88 --> 00:00:42.47
Selecting a stage shows its runs, its log, the files it committed,

00:00:42.47 --> 00:00:44.76
and the decisions its agent made.

00:00:45.11 --> 00:00:47.93
The log follows new lines as they arrive.

00:00:47.93 --> 00:00:52.20
Scroll up, and it holds still and counts what you have missed.

00:00:52.20 --> 00:00:57.42
And screen reader users hear stage changes, at most once every five seconds.

00:00:58.57 --> 00:01:01.56
Everything on the page comes from one stream.

00:01:01.56 --> 00:01:05.89
A change is stored with the next sequence number for its project,

00:01:05.89 --> 00:01:08.41
in the same save as the change itself.

00:01:08.41 --> 00:01:12.60
Then it is broadcast to the project's group on the SignalR hub.

00:01:12.60 --> 00:01:15.99
The client store applies each event once, in order,

00:01:15.99 --> 00:01:18.99
and fetches any it missed by sequence number.

00:01:19.34 --> 00:01:24.61
Journey three adds three events: step started, log lines, and decision recorded.

00:01:25.76 --> 00:01:30.47
Before each step, the worker names it, so the running stage can show it.

00:01:30.47 --> 00:01:33.42
Log lines no longer go one request at a time.

00:01:33.42 --> 00:01:38.53
The worker batches them every quarter of a second, up to five hundred at once,

00:01:38.53 --> 00:01:42.52
and always sends what it has before a checkpoint or a result.

00:01:42.52 --> 00:01:44.42
Each batch becomes one event.

00:01:44.77 --> 00:01:50.18
After a document stage commits, the worker reports the decisions it recorded,

00:01:50.18 --> 00:01:51.65
with their rationale.

00:01:51.65 --> 00:01:55.10
Hewn keeps a redacted copy for the Decisions tab,

00:01:55.10 --> 00:01:58.75
and ignores a decision a resumed step reports twice.

00:01:59.90 --> 00:02:04.53
The page loads the project once, then folds every event into it.

00:02:04.53 --> 00:02:08.23
A step started event sets the running stage's step.

00:02:08.23 --> 00:02:11.05
A log lines event sets its latest line.

00:02:11.05 --> 00:02:15.47
A stage changed event clears both, because the run has ended.

00:02:15.82 --> 00:02:19.79
Selecting a stage loads its runs, artifacts and decisions,

00:02:19.79 --> 00:02:23.21
and reloads them when an event touches that stage.

00:02:23.21 --> 00:02:27.79
The tabs work from the keyboard, with the arrow keys, Home and End.

00:02:28.94 --> 00:02:34.34
The log loads every stored line in pages, then merges new lines by line number,

00:02:34.34 --> 00:02:38.51
so a line that arrives early is neither lost nor shown twice.

00:02:38.51 --> 00:02:41.92
While the user is at the bottom, the view follows.

00:02:41.92 --> 00:02:45.41
Scrolled up, it stays put and counts the new lines.

00:02:45.76 --> 00:02:50.61
Above five hundred lines, the log renders only a window around the view,

00:02:50.61 --> 00:02:54.92
so no more than five hundred line elements are ever in the page.

00:02:54.92 --> 00:03:00.18
Each windowed line keeps to one row, so the spacers above and below are exact.

00:03:01.33 --> 00:03:05.20
The backend gained fourteen tests against the real API,

00:03:05.20 --> 00:03:07.87
and the worker six against a fake API.

00:03:07.87 --> 00:03:12.16
The backend and worker slices began with their tests failing.

00:03:12.16 --> 00:03:16.45
All green, the backend has one hundred and forty seven tests,

00:03:16.45 --> 00:03:19.40
and the worker one hundred and twenty six.

00:03:19.75 --> 00:03:22.50
The frontend has thirty five unit tests.

00:03:22.50 --> 00:03:28.15
End to end, five new pipeline tests drive real workers: a stage turning over live,

00:03:28.15 --> 00:03:33.60
the log holding when scrolled up, a past stage's tabs, a six thousand line log,

00:03:33.60 --> 00:03:35.94
and the five second announcements.

00:03:35.94 --> 00:03:41.45
Accessibility checks now cover every tab, and a visual test compares the waiting

00:03:41.45 --> 00:03:42.83
state with its mock.

00:03:43.98 --> 00:03:46.98
Here is a direction starting with one worker.

00:03:46.98 --> 00:03:51.85
The running stage shows its step and its latest line, both updating live.

00:03:51.85 --> 00:03:55.65
Bootstrap turns Succeeded, and Idea starts straight away.

00:03:56.00 --> 00:03:57.40
Here is the live log.

00:03:57.40 --> 00:03:58.79
It follows new lines.

00:03:58.79 --> 00:04:04.12
Scroll up, and it holds, with the count of new lines and a button to jump to the

00:04:04.12 --> 00:04:04.58
latest.

00:04:04.58 --> 00:04:06.71
One click, and it follows again.

00:04:07.06 --> 00:04:09.12
Now a stage that has finished.

00:04:09.12 --> 00:04:13.66
Selecting Idea shows its log, its run with the worker that ran it,

00:04:13.66 --> 00:04:17.85
the files it committed, and the decisions its agent recorded,

00:04:17.85 --> 00:04:19.50
each with its rationale.

00:04:19.85 --> 00:04:22.86
The same page works in dark mode and on a phone.

00:04:22.86 --> 00:04:25.87
And before any worker has picked up a direction,

00:04:25.87 --> 00:04:28.12
the page says it is waiting for one.

00:04:29.27 --> 00:04:31.05
Journey three is complete.

00:04:31.05 --> 00:04:35.83
Every stage change, step and log line reaches the page live, in order,

00:04:35.83 --> 00:04:37.54
from one numbered stream.

00:04:37.54 --> 00:04:41.77
The log follows, holds and stays light, however long it grows.

00:04:41.77 --> 00:04:45.32
And every stage shows its runs, files and decisions.

00:04:45.32 --> 00:04:48.26
Next comes journey four, limiting spending.
